            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0753" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg639"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1211/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-01T12:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                                1922—12 noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 5:07
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Your telegram number 9, January 25, 6 p.m. Pani states that the proposals are
                    to sign the first of the claims conventions <pb facs="0754" n="640"
                        xml:id="pg640"/> submitted by him whereby the Obregón Government will be
                    implicitly recognized, the second claims convention to be signed immediately
                    thereafter, and that after recognition General Obregón will take into
                    consideration any treaty of amity and commerce which may be submitted to be
                    studied and to be signed provided that it contains nothing opposed to the
                    fundamental laws of the country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
